  "acceptance": "Consume D12's abstract Sturm engine (Poincare/D12/ComparisonGeodesics/SturmComparison.lean: sturm_zero_comparison, wronskian_deriv, wronskian_antitoneOn_of_le) with CONSTRUCTED Jacobi data and produce a genuine zero-interlacing statement, not a restatement. Required content: (1) instantiate the engine with k1 = 1 (u1 = sin) and k2 = 0 (u2 = t) on (0,pi) to obtain that the first positive zero of sin is < pi, or the sharper two-curvature interlacing for k2 <= k1; (2) prove the zero-counting corollary: for K > 0 and k >= K, the first positive zero of a Jacobi solution with u 0 = 0, u' 0 = 1 (if it exists before a given horizon) is at most pi/sqrt(K), cross-checked against this round's conjugate_point_bound; (3) consume the Wronskian monotonicity with explicit data. Deliverable: compiling modules with full signatures, source hashes, compile exits, fail-closed axiom audit (cone subset {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}), non-vacuous witnesses, and a semantic review of expanded hypotheses. Existing inputs to reuse read-only: worktrees/leaders/L4-geometric-critical-path/release/Poincare/L4/GeodesicComparison/*.lean and Poincare/D12/ComparisonGeodesics/*.lean. Do not assume the target theorem as a hypothesis and do not duplicate the already-proved conjugate_point_bound.",
